19. Stage 1 Conclusion

Stage 1 defines TENTORA as an AI-powered creative-solutions platform with two connected ways to obtain a creative result.

Design Now

Sector → Service → Ready Interactive Design → Customization → Preview → Export

Work With a Creative

Sector → Services and Work → Project Needs → One Taste Test → Optional Service Direction → Up to Six Creative or Team Recommendations → Selection → Project Management → Delivery

The central product rules are:

Design Now begins with a ready interactive design, not a blank canvas or a full taste test.

Every custom project has one Main Taste Profile that applies to all selected services by default.

A service may have an optional direction without requiring the full taste test to be repeated.

Recommendation results are limited to six creative or team options.

Self-service work can move into professional creative execution without restarting the journey.

Ready-design creators retain attribution, ownership, and defined commercial rights.

This definition is the foundation for Stage 2, where the revised MVP scope, objectives, stakeholders, deliverables, risks, and success metrics will be formally approved.
